
TCS DIGITAL MASTER ROADMAP & SYLLABUS (2027)

Target Role: Digital Specialist Engineer (DSE)
Primary Programming Language: Python
Objective: Clear Advanced Quantitative Aptitude, Technical MCQs, and 2 Advanced Coding Questions within 60 minutes.

PART 1: COMPLETE PYTHON SYLLABUS


1. Python Fundamentals

• Python Basics: Introduction, Environment Setup, Syntax, Indentation, Comments, Variables, Input/Output (print(), input()), Type Conversion.
• Python Data Types:
	• Numeric: int, float, complex, bool
	• Text: str
	• Sequence: list, tuple, range
	• Set: set, frozenset
	• Mapping: dict
	• Binary: bytes, bytearray, memoryview
	• Special: NoneType
• Operators: Arithmetic, Comparison, Logical, Assignment, Bitwise (<<, >>, &, |, ^), Membership (in, not in), Identity (is, is not).
• Conditional Statements: if, if-else, if-elif-else, Nested if, match-case.
• Loops: for loop, while loop, Nested loops, Loop Control (break, continue, pass), range() function.

2. Intermediate & Advanced Python Concepts

• Functions: Definition, Calling, Parameters vs Arguments, Positional, Keyword, Default, Variable-length (*args, **kwargs), return statement, Scope (global, nonlocal), Lambda functions, Recursive functions.
• Python Collections: List methods, Tuple methods, Set methods, Dictionary methods, Nested collections, Mutable vs Immutable objects, Shallow copy vs Deep copy.
• Comprehensions: List Comprehension, Set Comprehension, Dictionary Comprehension.
• Built-in Functional Tooling: map(), filter(), reduce(), zip(), enumerate(), sorted(), any(), all().
• Advanced Mechanics: Iterators, Generators, Decorators, Exception Handling (try-except-finally), File Handling (open(), with), Modules, and Packages.

PART 2: DATA STRUCTURES & ALGORITHMS (TCS DIGITAL CORE)


1. Algorithm Analysis

• Time Complexity & Space Complexity.
• Asymptotic Notation: Big-O (O), Big-Omega (Ω), Big-Theta (Θ).
• Worst-case, Average-case, and Best-case complexity structures.
• Key Complexities to Memorize: O(1), \(O(\log n)\), O(n), \(O(n \log n)\), O(n²).

2. Arrays, Strings & Hashing

• Arrays: Python lists as dynamic arrays, Traversal, Insertion, Deletion, Searching, Reversing, Rotating, Prefix/Suffix Sums, Subarrays.
• Strings: Immutability, Indexing, Slicing, Frequency Counting, Anagram check, Palindrome verification, Substring manipulation.
• Hashing: Hash Tables via Dictionaries/Sets, Collision basics, O(1) lookup optimizations.

3. Core Techniques & Non-Linear Structures

• Two-Pointer Technique: Converging pointers (left/right), Fast & Slow pointers.
• Sliding Window: Fixed-size and Variable-size windows.
• Searching & Sorting: Linear Search, Binary Search (Iterative/Recursive, Rotated Sorted Arrays), Bubble Sort, Selection Sort, Insertion Sort, Merge Sort, Quick Sort.
• Matrices (2D Arrays): Row/Column/Diagonal traversals, Transpose, Spiral Traversal.
• Linear Data Structures (MCQ Focus): Stacks (LIFO), Queues (FIFO), Linked Lists (Singly, Doubly, Cycle Detection).
• Trees & BST (MCQ Focus): Traversals (Inorder, Preorder, Postorder, Level-Order), BST Properties, Height calculation.

