PART 4: COMPUTER SCIENCE FUNDAMENTALS (MCQ FOCUS)


1. Object-Oriented Programming (OOP)

• Classes, Objects, Attributes, and Methods.
• Constructors (__init__), Instance vs Class variables, and Static methods.
• The Four Pillars: Inheritance (Single, Multiple, Multilevel, Hierarchical), Polymorphism (Method Overriding vs Overloading concepts), Encapsulation (Private attributes), and Abstraction.

2. DBMS & SQL

• DBMS vs RDBMS architecture.
• Keys: Primary Key, Foreign Key, Candidate Key, Super Key, Composite Key.
• Data Normalization: 1NF, 2NF, 3NF.
• ACID properties and Transaction control.
• Core SQL Commands: SELECT, DISTINCT, WHERE, ORDER BY, LIMIT, GROUP BY, HAVING.
• SQL Joins: INNER, LEFT, RIGHT, FULL OUTER, SELF joins.
• Advanced Analytics: Subqueries, Correlated subqueries, CTEs, and Window Functions (ROW_NUMBER(), RANK(), DENSE_RANK()).

3. Operating Systems & Computer Networks

• OS: Processes vs Threads, Context Switching, CPU Scheduling algorithms (FCFS, SJF, Round Robin, Priority).
• Deadlocks (4 necessary conditions, prevention). Memory management (Paging, Virtual Memory, Segmentation).
• Networks: OSI Model vs TCP/IP Model layers.
• Protocols: TCP vs UDP, HTTP vs HTTPS, DNS lookup, IP vs MAC addressing, Port mappings.
• Software Engineering: SDLC models (Waterfall vs Agile Scrum), Software Testing strategies, Git/GitHub version control workflows.

